| If the question says...        | Pattern                 | Data Structure    |
| ------------------------------ | ----------------------- | ----------------- |
| Every subarray of size K       | Fixed Window            | Variables         |
| Maximum sum of size K          | Fixed Window            | Variables         |
| Longest substring              | Variable Window         | HashSet / HashMap |
| Smallest subarray              | Variable Window         | Variables         |
| At most K distinct             | Variable Window         | HashMap           |
| Count distinct in every window | Fixed Window            | HashMap           |
| First negative in every window | Fixed Window            | Queue             |
| Maximum in every window        | Fixed Window            | Deque             |
| Exactly K                      | AtMost(K) − AtMost(K−1) | HashMap/Variables |

1. Brute Force – O(n²)
Idea: Generate every possible subarray and check whether it satisfies the condition.
2. Sliding Window – O(n)
Instead of generating every subarray, use two pointers (left and right) and maintain a valid window.
This approach is useful when the condition allows us to expand and shrink the window efficiently.
3. Exactly K = AtMost(K) - AtMost(K-1)
Idea: Sometimes directly counting exactly K is difficult. So we calculate two easier answers and subtract them.
Exactly(K)=AtMost(K)-AtMost(K-1)

                
